<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5" extension="2015-08-01"/><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5.1" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Gradual, painless blurring of vision in both eyes over about two years, worse in the right, with glare from sunlight and oncoming headlights, faded colors, and trouble recognizing faces across a room; Snellen acuity 20/200 right and 20/100 left with his old glasses, no better with a pinhole; no flashes, floaters, pain or redness; cause under evaluation with an ophthalmology consultation</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>H54.3</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented failing eyesight; superseded when the consultation found bilateral cataract.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Bilateral age-related nuclear cataract, dense and brunescent in the right eye and moderate in the left, with cortical spokes; the cause of his reduced vision, glare and color loss; no glaucoma, macular degeneration or diabetic retinopathy; treated with sequential cataract surgery</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>H25.13</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the consultation, linked to his documented loss of sight; not a retrospective diagnosis of his real blindness, whose cause is not recorded.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Chronic low back pain for many years, aching across the lower back and worst on the side of an old arrow-wound scar over the right lower back, stiff in the morning and after long rides in his truck; no leg pain, numbness, weakness, bladder or bowel change, fever or weight loss; no red flags</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M54.59</td><td>S — Synthetic chronic back pain anchored to his documented arrow wound; which side of the back the arrowhead lay in is not recorded, and the right side is a synthetic choice.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Nontoxic multinodular goiter, present for decades: a firm, nodular, non-tender thyroid enlargement with no pressure symptoms (no trouble swallowing or breathing, no voice change); euthyroid</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E04.2</td><td>S — Synthetic modern classification of his documented goiter; the type of his real goiter is not recorded.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Primary osteoarthritis of both knees, aching on stairs and after walking the orchard, with morning stiffness under half an hour, crepitus and bony enlargement</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M17.0</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis anchored to his documented rheumatism; the old term does not name a modern diagnosis.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>One fall in the past year, missing the bottom step of the porch at dusk, without injury; poor vision in low light and contrast; at risk of further falls</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z91.81</td><td>S — Synthetic fall linked to the reduced vision.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-7">
    <td>Sprain of the right wrist from a fall on the porch steps three weeks after the first cataract operation, when the two eyes saw differently; X-ray without fracture; healed</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>S63.501A</td><td>S — Synthetic acute injury at the sick visit; not a historical claim.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-8">
    <td>Lens implants in both eyes after sequential phacoemulsification cataract surgery, right then left six weeks apart; best-corrected vision about 20/20 in each eye with new glasses</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z96.1</td><td>S — Synthetic status after the modern cataract surgery.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

