    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic low back pain (M54.59)</content>. Pain down from 6 to 2 out of 10 over six months with exercise therapy, without opioids or other pain tablets. [S]<list><item>Continue the home program and tai chi; return if pain flares for more than a few weeks or any red flag appears.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Multinodular goiter (E04.2)</content>. Stable on examination, with no pressure symptoms. [S]<list><item>Repeat thyroid ultrasound in about 18 months; TSH if symptoms change.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Falls (Z91.81)</content>. No falls since the spring; good vision, handrails and exercise. [S]<list><item>Keep the step edging and lights; a neighbor or helper steadies the ladder.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Back pain intensity (0 to 10) and function</td><td>Every visit while treatment is adjusted</td><td>Completed today</td><td>2 out of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Red flags: leg weakness or numbness, bladder or bowel change, fever, weight loss</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise therapy (physical therapy, then a home program)</td><td>From diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Home program most mornings; tai chi weekly</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Pain medicines: no opioids or muscle relaxants; oral NSAID only if needed and safe</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No pain tablets</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Thyroid function (TSH, free T4)</td><td>If symptoms change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>TSH 1.62 and free T4 1.2 at intake; no symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Thyroid ultrasound with nodule pattern; biopsy only by size and pattern thresholds</td><td>At evaluation of a goiter; repeat in 12 to 24 months for nodules below biopsy thresholds</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Next ultrasound in about 18 months</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Pressure symptoms (swallowing, breathing, voice) and neck examination</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No pressure symptoms; goiter unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Comprehensive dilated eye examination (pupils, slit lamp, dilated lens and fundus)</td><td>Before surgery to confirm cataract as the cause; then every one to two years at 65 and older</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Next comprehensive eye examination in one to two years</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Falls: falls since the last visit, Timed Up and Go, home hazards</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; Timed Up and Go 10 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Knee pain and function; exercise; topical diclofenac use and skin</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Gel after long days; no skin irritation</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Mood (PHQ-9)</td><td>At intake and when vision or function changes</td><td>Completed today</td><td>1, from 4, with item 9 scored 0</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Find the cause of the blurred vision. Outcome by 2026-04-21: Bilateral age-related cataract; glaucoma, macular degeneration and diabetic retinopathy excluded [S]</item><item>See well enough to recognize faces, walk safely at dusk and meet the vision standard for driving. Outcome by 2026-07-21: Best-corrected vision about 20/20 in each eye after sequential surgery; cleared to drive by day and night [S]</item><item>No falls with injury. In progress; target 2027-04-07 [S]</item><item>Back pain at 3 or less out of 10 and back to a full day in the orchard. Outcome by 2026-09-29: Average pain 6 to 2 out of 10 on exercise therapy without opioids [S]</item><item>Keep the goiter under watch without unnecessary tests. In progress; target 2028-04-21 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Cataract in the Adult Eye Preferred Practice Pattern (2021); Noninvasive Treatments for Acute, Subacute, and Chronic Low Back Pain: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians (2017); 2015 American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Thyroid Nodules and Differentiated Thyroid Cancer (2015); 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, cataract and rheumatoid arthritis/osteoarthritis monographs (2026); Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Second zoster dose and influenza and COVID-19 vaccines this autumn. Thyroid ultrasound in about 18 months. Eye examination in one to two years. Next wellness visit in a year, sooner as needed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
